---
export const prerender = true;
import '../../../styles/global.css';
import '../../../styles/cai-doc.css';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
  <title>Cultivated AI · Part One · Pre-workshop interview · The Baker's Dozen</title>
  <style>
    .cd-q-type {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.58rem; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--bar, var(--doc-accent));
      margin-left: 0.5rem;
      vertical-align: 0.1em;
      opacity: 0.8;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="cd-shell" style="--doc-accent: var(--color-amber);">

    <div class="cd-printhint screen-only">
      <span class="accent">Send or print →</span>
      Share this as a doc, or press <kbd>⌘ P</kbd> for a clean PDF. Sixteen questions, about fifteen minutes.
    </div>

    <p class="cd-eyebrow">Cultivated AI · Part One · before we begin</p>
    <h1 class="cd-title">Tell us how you <em>actually work</em>.</h1>
    <p class="cd-lede">This workshop runs on <strong>your own real tasks</strong>, not sample ones. The more honestly you answer, the more the two days are built around the decisions you own. Nothing here is a test. About fifteen minutes.</p>
    <p class="cd-meta">16 questions · ~15 min · one per leader · The Baker's Dozen</p>
    <div class="cd-rule"></div>

    <!-- ── About you ── -->
    <section class="cd-section is-amber">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Part 01</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">About <em>you</em></h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q01</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">What's your role, and what are you actually accountable for week to week?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We tune every example to the decisions you own, not your job title.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q02</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Walk us through a typical week. Where does your time really go?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We want to aim at the hours that repeat, because those are the ones AI can give back.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q03</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">From "tried it once" to "it's in my daily work," where are you with AI today? <span class="cd-q-type">Scale 1–5</span></p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">This places you on the ladder so we pitch the room at the right level.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ── How you work with AI today ── -->
    <section class="cd-section is-teal">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Part 02</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">How you work with AI <em>today</em></h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q04</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Which AI tools do you use now, if any, and what for?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We meet you where you are and fix what is already half-working before adding anything new.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q05</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">What's the best result you've ever gotten from AI? And the worst?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Your real wins and failures are the most useful teaching material we have.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q06</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">When you <em>don't</em> use AI for something you could, what stops you? <span class="cd-q-type">Pick + explain</span></p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Time, trust, not knowing how, or data sensitivity. The honest blocker is what we design around.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Your real work ── -->
    <section class="cd-section is-purple">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Part 03</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">Your real work <em>(the tasks we'll build on)</em></h2>
      </div>
      <p class="cd-section-blurb">These answers become your live exercises in the room, and most likely your first skills. Bring specifics.</p>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q07</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Name three tasks you do over and over that you'd hand off tomorrow if you trusted the output.</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">These are the strongest candidates for your first reusable skills.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q08</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">What's one report, email, or deck you dread making? Bring a real, anonymised example.</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We will rebuild it with you, live, during the workshop.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q09</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">What question about the business do you wish you could just ask and get answered instantly?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">This sharpens what "AI-forward" means for you, and seeds Part Two, Mission Control.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Your team and function ── -->
    <section class="cd-section is-sky">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Part 04</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">Your team and <em>function</em></h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q10</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">How big is your team, and how AI-comfortable are they, honestly?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We plan skill-sharing around the real starting line, not the ideal one.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q11</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Which parts of your function should AI <em>never</em> touch, in your view?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Knowing where AI does not belong is half of the framework we teach.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q12</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">If one workflow in your team got five times faster, which one would matter most to the business?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We point the 90-day plan at impact, not novelty.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ── The people side ── -->
    <section class="cd-section is-red">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Part 05</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">The <em>people</em> side</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q13</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">When your team hears "AI is coming," what do you think they actually feel?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Rollouts fail on fear, not tooling. We address it directly, and you set the tone.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q14</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">What would make this workshop a clear win for you, in one sentence?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">We will hold ourselves to your definition of success, not ours.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Readiness ── -->
    <section class="cd-section is-navy">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Part 06</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">Readiness</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="cd-qlist">
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q15</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Which account will you bring (ChatGPT, Claude, or Gemini), and is it free or paid?</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">So we confirm everyone can run every exercise. See the pre-requisites list for details.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-q"><span class="cd-q-num">Q16</span><div>
          <p class="cd-q-text">Anything we should know to make the room work for you? Access, language, accessibility, anything.</p>
          <p class="cd-q-why">Small adjustments are easy when we know in advance.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <div class="cd-callout" style="--bar: var(--color-amber); margin-top: 2.75rem;">
      <h4>Before the first session</h4>
      <p>Send your answers back, and have the account from Q15 signed in and ready. That's all. We'll do the rest.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cd-footer">
      <span class="brand">Cultivated AI · <em>Grow, don't Chase.</em></span>
      <span>Part One · pre-workshop interview</span>
    </div>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
